 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "PLACEMENT\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 2, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Object\n   2 Object path\n   3 Object speed\n   4 Object in frame\n   5 Number of people\n   6 Where they stand\n   7 Eyelines\n   8 Who is sharp\n   9 Look of the actor\n  10 Empty frame\n  11 Foreshortening\n  12 Who stands higher\n  13 Who is closest to the camera\n  14 A line between them\n  15 Facing us or turned away\n  16 Standing apart from the others\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 2, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Power staging\n   2 suite: Alone in the frame\n   3 suite: Dinner table scene\n   4 suite: Glamour close-up\n   5 suite: Hushed two-hander\n   6 suite: Car chase\n   7 suite: Looming over them\n   8 suite: Growing apart\n   9 suite: The outsider\n  10 pair: When an object enters, the frame becomes an insert\n  11 pair: When people get closer, they hold each other's look\n  12 pair: When something looms at the lens, the audience flinches\n  13 pair: When a door is in the shot, someone comes through it\n  14 pair: When the focus moves to a door, someone is about to come in\n  15 pair: When food is on the table, people talk with their mouths full\n  16 pair: When an object moves fast, it smears into a blur\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 2, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When an object drops, a sound hit lands with it\n   2 pair: When an actor's look is striking, the camera holds on them longer\n   3 pair: When more people fill the scene, the sound gets busy\n   4 pair: When more people are in the scene, it needs more angles\n   5 pair: When one stands higher, the gap in rank grows\n   6 pair: When the height gap flips, the power flips\n   7 pair: When the near one fills more of the frame, the eye goes there first\n   8 pair: When the near one hides the other, more is kept from us\n   9 pair: When the line between them grows stronger, their feelings drift apart\n  10 pair: When someone steps across the line, warmth returns\n  11 pair: When they turn further away, what they mean drifts from what they say\n  12 pair: When they turn away to hide tears, we feel with them\n  13 pair: When they stand further from the group, loneliness grows\n  14 pair: When someone defies the group, they end up standing apart\n  15 pair: When the group comes to the one apart, warmth grows\n  16 pairs: Closing in\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 2, CC 97 to 100\n   1 pairs: Dinner gets messy\n   2 pairs: Speed and impact\n   3 pairs: Left out, then let in\n   4 pairs: The turn of power"
   },
